{"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"run","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"on","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"world","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A system depends on the systems before it that it must run after, by an ","type":"text"},{"code":"after","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" constraint, and on those it conflicts with: one writes what the other reads or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes, or either has no ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","type":"reference"},{"text":". The systems run in waves: each wave holds the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"systems whose dependencies all ran in earlier waves, and runs them with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"WorldModule\/World\/runConcurrently(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A system without an access runs alone. The world","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends as it would running the systems one after another in order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"At the start of each wave, every condition of its systems is checked, so a condition reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only what its system’s access lists, and the world’s change tick advances. Each system’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WorldModule\/World\/lastRun"},{"type":"text","text":" is the tick of its previous run, so filters such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".changed(Position.self)"},{"type":"text","text":" show it what changed since then: changes made by the systems"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after it on the previous run and before it on this one, but not its own. A system that has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not run on this world before sees every component as added and changed. A skipped system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has not run: the next time it runs, it sees everything since it last did."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before the first wave, each system that has not run on this world is initialized"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/initialize(in:)"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Command buffers the wave’s systems queue (","type":"text"},{"code":"WorldModule\/World\/queue(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") apply at the end","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the wave, in the order the systems run. The tick advances once more after the last wave,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so changes made to the world between runs are newer than every system’s previous run.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every system with an access reads and writes only what it lists; see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"WorldModule\/World\/runConcurrently(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Runs every system once on ","type":"text"},{"code":"world","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", running systems that do not depend on each other at the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same time.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7Systems8ScheduleV3run2ony11WorldModule0E0Vz_tF","title":"run(on:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"run","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"on","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Schedule.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/Schedule.swift#L162"},"modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/run(on:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"abstract":[{"text":"Rules that run on a world, in the order written unless constrained otherwise.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","title":"Systems","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems","role":"collection"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","title":"access","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","required":true,"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What the system reads and writes, so "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" can run it alongside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"systems it does not conflict with; nil, the default, when it may change anything and must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run alone."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"access","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Access","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"defaultImplementations":1},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems that run on a world, as though in the order written, at the same time where they can."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Schedule","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/initialize(in:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"initialize(in:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"initialize"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","text":"World"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/initialize(in:)","abstract":[{"text":"Prepares ","type":"text"},{"code":"world","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the system, before its first run on it: a schedule calls this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before the wave the system first runs in, outside any concurrent run. Nothing, by default.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/initialize(in:)","kind":"symbol","defaultImplementations":1,"required":true},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"World"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Entities, the components they hold, and the world’s resources."}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world","title":"World","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"World"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/run(on:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/run(on:)","title":"run(on:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs every system once on "},{"code":"world","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", running systems that do not depend on each other at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same time."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"run"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"on"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"World","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]}}}